"received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "199887023", "author": {"steamid": "76561198047925105", "personaname": "Shooty", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/narapoia/", "num_games_owned": 45, "num_reviews": 16, "playtime_forever": 472, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 375, "last_played": 1754100908, "avatar": "84dc58ca1a2f3de775438c40336986687a1af72c"}, "language": "english", "review": "FPS Gameplay in the style of Doom, visuals and weapon variety a la Borderlands, and a roguelite experience akin to Dead Cells. This game is fun as hell.", "timestamp_created": 1752612111, "timestamp_updated": 1752612111, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "199873485", "author": {"steamid": "76561198851751835", "personaname": "kijiko", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/kijikoyuri/", "num_games_owned": 190, "num_reviews": 73, "playtime_forever": 9343, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6550, "last_played": 1779544357, "avatar": "c73a54559acf06088f5b106c5ebb3583dd0c0dea"}, "language": "english", "review": "fantastic video game. really to boot up, slam down a couple of bots, maybe win a run if you lucky.\n\nevery single part of Roboquest just... works. its guns are some of the best in the rougelike FPS sphere, with only a few meh options, its style is cute and charming, inspired by stuff like Borderlands but doesn't assault the eyeballs (unlike the 3rd installment of that series), and its design shows that the team knew what they were doing, which is honestly surprising for a debut title. \n\nyou can play each difficulty and still get the same experience, no diff gating here. i did try to beat each difficulty after beating the game on the lowest one, and i got to normal. good deal of challenge if you want it.\n\nif there is a negative to Roboquest, its probably the Endless mode. its just not very good. i would suggest playing it if you have a uncureable addiction to the game, otherwise regular mode will have you sorted forever.\n\ngood game, and i hope that the next project from this team kicks as much ass as this one does.\n\n", "timestamp_created": 1752599994, "timestamp_updated": 1752599994, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "199864048", "author": {"steamid": "76561197975253720", "personaname": "Unforgiven", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/unforgiven91/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 144, "playtime_forever": 976, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 976, "last_played": 1751850105, "avatar": "553d9813756b290ea688fa7b311d1fe187565807"}, "language": "english", "review": "Fast, franctic and fun. I really enjoyed roboquest. Like Doom meets borderlands\r\n\r\nThe one complaint I ended up having was that co-op stopped being an ideal way to play. You and your buddybot end up working on different things and being together wasn't the ideal way to accomplish your goals by the end of it.", "timestamp_created": 1752592012, "timestamp_updated": 1752592012, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, 